    },
    {
      "position": 12,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "In a 少し example (#4927), 「水を少しくださし。」「いいですよ。」, くださし is written instead of ください. Is this a typo or is there a reason for it?",
      "html": "In a 少し example (#4927), 「水を少しくださし。」「いいですよ。」, くださし is written instead of ください. Is this a typo or is there a reason for it?",
      "credits_raw": "darkseed",
      "content_sha256": "32adc04e78127bb4aa1bb82b46dc35d141401e0d67a9783d177c80a1e133e392",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 13,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "This entry seems to have been tuned from level 4 to level 2. It seems to easy to be level 2. Please tune it back to level 3. どうぞ三級に戻って下さいませんか。",
      "html": "This entry seems to have been tuned from level 4 to level 2. It seems to easy to be level 2. Please tune it back to level 3. どうぞ三級に戻って下さいませんか。",
      "credits_raw": "赤毛",
      "content_sha256": "ac021ca907706ac466b701c0d16e90b34a00678181fd4326468561098cf02723",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 14,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I went through the examples and replaced 下 with くだ. Japanese manuals of style say to use the kanji with NOUNを下さい, contrasted with the TE-form VERBてください, in which you do not use the kanji.\n\nIt's not technically incorrect, but it's preferred, similar to how in English spelling out zero through ten is preferred, but using numbers for values greater than ten is preferred.",
      "html": "I went through the examples and replaced 下 with くだ. Japanese manuals of style say to use the kanji with NOUNを下さい, contrasted with the TE-form VERBてください, in which you do not use the kanji.<br/><br/>It's not technically incorrect, but it's preferred, similar to how in English spelling out zero through ten is preferred, but using numbers for values greater than ten is preferred.",
      "credits_raw": "KyleGoetz",
      "content_sha256": "11399f3b4ea59952565028cfce578be0ce6be167623b624d82a7a2b91a8a6ae4",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 15,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "How does onegai compare to kudasai in usage? Can a description and demonstration be added into this article, or does it need a separate page?",
